# From rung 7 to the real thing

### Every rung, found again in tutors-mono-repo

Week 12, the Summit. Talk 1

---

## You have climbed a straight line

1 Seed, 2 Lite, 3 Layers, 4 Proven, 5 Reader, 6 Guarded, 7 Shipped.

- Each rung was a copy of the one below, plus one capability
- So rung 7 holds all seven: a generator, a site, layers, a specification, a reader, defences, a release
- Each capability mirrors part of the real repository

This talk maps each rung to its upstream home, then shows what the real repository adds that no rung covers.
All paths are at the pinned commit `2b96b69` of tutors-sdk/tutors-mono-repo.

---

## This week's outcomes

- **(Analyse)** Map each rung to the upstream areas it mirrors, and classify what the mono-repo adds
- **(Evaluate)** Judge at which Assertion Ladder level upstream keeps a rule
- **(Evaluate)** Choose a small improvement by its value, at a rung you have finished
- **(Create)** Specify it first, in upstream's own style, and fence your agent
- **(Create)** Implement it, run the gates, defend it on an A3

Lean focus: **Kaizen upstream**. One small improvement to someone else's standard work.

---

## Rungs 1 to 3: the generator and its architecture

| Rung | Variant | Upstream areas |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 Seed | `rung-1-seed` | `packages/jsr/gen`, `packages/jsr/model`, `packages/jsr/tutors` |
| 2 Lite | `rung-2-lite` | `packages/jsr/tutors-lite` |
| 3 Layers | `rung-3-layers` | `pnpm-workspace.yaml`, `packages/jsr/types`, the ports in `packages/jsr/course-rules`, `tests/architecture` |

Upstream adds: `packages/jsr/create` (the scaffolder and `tutors validate`), `packages/jsr/tutors-cli` (one
program for every tool), and dependency-cruiser rules in `.dependency-cruiser.cjs`.

